    {
      "el": "Fleet when it is part paused: two of four queues are paused, the console and the service read different Valkeys, and an operator works out what is stuck and what to start again.",
      "kind": "readme",
      "status": "new",
      "source": "admin/src/console/panels/fleet.mjs#fleetBar",
      "golden": [
        "panels/fleet-part-paused.operator"
      ],
      "shows": [
        "Part paused",
        "Starts nothing new:",
        "Keeps starting jobs:"
      ],
      "panel": "p-fleetbar"
    },
    {
      "el": "**The fleet bar.** It is ringed yellow and says *Part paused* with which queues start nothing new and which keep going. Its counts add *in paused queues*. Both switches are offered: *Resume the fleet* (paid, amber outline, because queued jobs start spending) and *Pause the fleet* (danger).",
      "kind": "readme",
      "status": "new",
      "source": "admin/src/console/panels/fleet.mjs#fleetBar",
      "golden": [
        "panels/fleet-part-paused.operator"
      ],
      "shows": [
        "Part paused",
        "in paused queues",
        "Resume the fleet",
        "Pause the fleet",
        "card--ring"
      ],
      "panel": "p-fleetbar"
    },
    {
      "el": "**Two Valkeys.** When `VALKEY_URL` differs between the console's environment and the deployment's `.env`, a yellow line says so in the repo's words. A pause reaches both; a resume is refused, and the refusal opens where the preview would, with the command that resumes one Valkey on purpose. Nothing was changed.",
      "kind": "readme",
      "status": "new",
      "source": "admin/src/console/panels/fleet.mjs#fleetBar",
      "golden": [
        "panels/fleet-two-valkeys.operator"
      ],
      "shows": [
        "Two Valkeys",
        "Refused: Resume the fleet",
        "Nothing was changed",
        "--valkey-url",
        "Copy"
      ],
      "panel": "p-fleetbar"
    },
    {
      "el": "**Queues.** Paused rows are tinted and say *Paused* with the pause glyph. Their sub-line says the host still takes shared jobs. *Resume* on a row is paid; its preview names how many jobs wait in it and why no single reserve figure applies.",
      "kind": "readme",
      "status": "new",
      "source": "admin/src/console/panels/fleet.mjs#fleetQueues",
      "golden": [
        "panels/fleet-part-paused.operator"
      ],
      "shows": [
        "Paused",
        "Resume",
        "Its host still takes shared jobs."
      ],
      "panel": "p-queues"
    },
    {
      "el": "**Failed jobs.** Each row quotes its run record's sentence. The bulk editor filters by queue or repository; *Retry all* opens a preview that lists each job with its reserve, then the bulk reserve, including the case where one job's reserve is unknown. *Why each failed* shows the queue's own text in a collapsed row per job.",
      "kind": "readme",
      "status": "new",
      "source": "admin/src/console/panels/fleet.mjs#fleetFailed",
      "golden": [
        "panels/fleet-part-paused.operator"
      ],
      "shows": [
        "Its run record says:",
        "Only queue",
        "Only repository",
        "Retry all",
        "Remove all",
        "Why each failed"
      ],
      "panel": "p-failed"
    },
    {
      "el": "**Held.** Each held job's condition label as the worker writes it (`after … + ci-green`), how long it has waited and how many of its 96 checks it has used.",
      "kind": "readme",
      "status": "new",
      "source": "admin/src/console/panels/fleet.mjs#fleetHeld",
      "golden": [
        "panels/fleet-part-paused.operator"
      ],
      "shows": [
        "ci-green",
        "checks",
        "held",
        "class=\"fl-held\""
      ],
      "panel": "p-held"
    },
    {
      "el": "**Delayed.** The delayed count is one number. The card splits out what can be counted (cron next occurrences, held jobs) and calls the rest *undifferentiated*. A folded list explains every deferral and how often it asks again. Jobs waiting for a host budget link to the host.",
      "kind": "readme",
      "status": "new",
      "source": "admin/src/console/panels/fleet.mjs#fleetDelayed",
      "golden": [
        "panels/fleet-part-paused.operator"
      ],
      "shows": [
        "cron schedules",
        "held jobs",
        "reason their worker recorded",
        "What can delay a job"
      ],
      "panel": "p-delayed"
    },
    {
      "el": "**Other states.** Running, paused (kill switch on), a pause that did not reach every queue, an unreadable host registry, a held set too large to read, and the per-job results after a bulk retry with *Reload*.",
      "kind": "readme",
      "status": "new",
      "source": "admin/src/console/panels/fleet.mjs#fleetBar",
      "golden": [
        "panels/fleet-part-paused.operator"
      ],
